<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Long-term
prepayment of US$<span id="xdx_903_eus-gaap--PrepaidExpenseNoncurrent_iI_pn4n6_c20250630_zDc4uWz1JrXb" title="Long-term prepayment"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:PrepaidExpenseNoncurrent" contextRef="AsOf2025-06-30" id="Fact001629" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-4" scale="6" unitRef="USD">3.04</ix:nonFraction></span> million were mainly attributable to the advances paid to FAW Jilin&#8217;s suppliers for molds and tool manufacturing
of car body and vehicle parts. These expenditures will be capitalized as property, plant and equipment after molds and tools reach the
working condition for its intended use.</span></p>

